"""layers.1.mlp.down_proj:4581, a component that is near zero almost everywhere.

Its large values come from three kinds of token, all of them cases where the token
has no real context to draw on:

1. The first token of each document (or of a packed row that starts mid-document).
   Its value depends on what kind of token it is:
   - bare separators, closing punctuation and blank or newline-only tokens
     (",", ".", ";", ")", '",', ".\\n", "  ") are strongly negative, about -2.8;
   - digits are about -1;
   - words (letters, with or without a leading space) are mildly negative, -0.4;
   - openers and operators ("#", "[", "|", "=", "//") are about 0.

