   space in front of a digit after a run of spaces ("   21" is "  ", " ", "2", "1"),
   so this is the padding before a line or column number in a numbered listing or an
   aligned table. It is about -1.45. A lone space after another lone space is about -0.46.

3. Runs of middle dots (dot leaders, "····"), always about -0.66.

Every other position is predicted as 0. The program is stateless: it only looks at the
current token and the one before it, and at whether a document has just started.
